      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1251946045">
          <groundspeak:date>2024-08-08T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP190 Calgary - Edworthy Park [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks to a certain log from 2014 I was able to widen my radius in the proper direction for an easy find (well, easy when you know where it is!) TFTCap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="1040787410">
          <groundspeak:date>2020-06-17T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7269274">WhyWhySee</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP190 Calgary - Edworthy Park [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Found when a nearby cache was posted with a waypoint for this brass cap, but didn't know what to do with it then! https://coord.info/GL11QC73P&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="935240076">
          <groundspeak:date>2020-06-09T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Write note</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="265062">nicolo</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP190 - Calgary ( Edworthy Park III )

N 51° 03.563 W 114° 09.278&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I snagged this Cap back in April of 2005 with another cacher or two. j2d2 had snagged the FTF the previous day. I thought that he was with us that day 🤷‍♂️ ... sooooo I'm getting old I guess, bad memory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anywho, after finding a really nicely hidden nearby geocache I arrived here and started to search, and search, and search! Ugh, my capping skills are rusty and, to top it off, I lost my long, thing screwdriver that I use to poke for caps at the previous geocache (I assume).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fortunately I had my compass with me and after a bunch of compass sweeping, some falsely dug mini-holes, and referencing my old pictures the Cap was revealed, about 1 inch BGL ... it was last found by OBA in April of 2017 so I guess that a few years made a difference!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Took a few pics, great spot for views of Bow Valley, covered the Cap with a rock, and headed home.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So if you've never found this Cap, now's a good time (and great weather) to snag this one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A good day 🤷‍♂️🤷‍♂️&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682800528">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP190 Edworthy Park &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It was a tough find but Iron Phoenix and I were still laughing as we looked. On our way to the cache someone called Pippin (my geo dog) a walking pillow &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks to Outforthehunt for maintaining the Brass Cap cache for everyone to enjoy!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682505930">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP190 - Edworthy Park&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I managed to convince One Bad Ant that with the impending doom.... er, I mean, the upcoming change in logging rules, that we should do a multi-day blitzing of Brass Caps! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Of course silly us, we came at it from the bottom of the hill.  It didn't look THAT far up. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_blackeye.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Oh well, we got there, survived, and the furry cacher had a great time helping out (as usual) Apparently it was reported to be a bit difficult to find with the coords bouncing, but I found that where I had stopped to look at my GPSr when it was telling me I was 0m-1m away, I just needed to turn around and take a step and I was on top of it! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; It's in pretty good shape - a few scratches but just fine. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
    </groundspeak:cache>
  </wpt>
